        "original_id": "8819f56a-80ac-5129-adea-fb66b665b5c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Children’s National Medical Center, MedStar Washington Hospital Center, MedStar Health, Georgetown University School of Medicine, Georgetown University Hospital, Children’s Research Institute, Center for Cancer and Immunology Research\n- People: Anthony Sandler\n- Places: Washington, D.C., Washington metropolitan area\n- Roles: Chief of Pediatric Surgery, Principal Investigator\n\nFacts:\n- Children’s National Medical Center, formerly DC Children’s Hospital, is ranked among the top 10 children’s hospitals in the United States by U.S. News & World Report.\n- MedStar Washington Hospital Center is the largest private hospital in Washington, D.C.\n- MedStar Washington Hospital Center is a member of MedStar Health and is licensed for 926 beds.\n- Georgetown University School of Medicine works in association with the 609-bed Georgetown University Hospital, Washington Hospital Center, and nine other affiliated federal and community hospitals in the Washington metropolitan area.\n- Anthony Sandler is the Chief of Pediatric Surgery at Children’s National Medical Center.\n- Anthony Sandler also serves as a Principal Investigator in the Children’s Research Institute and the Center for Cancer and Immunology Research at Children’s National Medical Center.",
